// @emit-error emitProgram: struct field type `u8[]` has no struct-field rep
// THE WORSE FACE of `error-u8-field-through-generic-alias.vl`: with the field never READ,
// the mis-interned module VALIDATED. `vl build` exited 0, wasmtime instantiated it, the
// program printed 1, and the emitted rec group carried BOTH backings —
//
//     (type 0 (struct (field (mut (ref 2)))))          ; Box<u8[]>, field `v`
//     (type 1 (array (mut i32)))  (type 2 (struct …))  ; the i32-list wrapper it got
//     (type 3 (array (mut i8)))   (type 4 (struct …))  ; the PACKED pair `u8[]` needs
//
// — the field wired to the wrong one of the two. Nothing in the program touched the field,
// so nothing forced the two to meet, and the only symptom was a shape that would fail the
// validator the moment anyone read it (the sibling file).
//
// A latent wrong rep behind a valid module is not a smaller bug than an invalid one; it is
// the same bug with the witness deleted. This file keeps the witness.
type Box<T> = { v: T }

const b: Box<u8[]> = { v: [7] }
print(1)
